; Like Bison's error recovery, beancount's parser reports no syntax error
; until three tokens have been shifted after the last one, reported or not.
; A line break counts as a token, and so does the indent of an indented line;
; a comment does not. Invalid tokens are its lexer's errors, always reported.
"stray"
"suppressed: right after an error"

2020-01-04 * "y" ^
"suppressed: right after an invalid token"

2020-01-02 open Assets:B USD USD USD
"suppressed: right after an error"
; comment
"suppressed: a comment line is one line break"


"reported: three line breaks after an error"
2020-01-01 open Assets:A
"reported: a valid directive in between"
2020-01-01 "suppressed: two tokens in"
2020-01-01 open "reported: three tokens in"
"suppressed"
  Assets:A
"suppressed: an indented line is an error too"
"suppressed" ^
